            <div xml:id="d357">

                <pb facs="0390" n="382" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg382"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">391.1163/125b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Iran</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-20T20:00:00-05:00">December 20, 1941—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>161. The Department has transmitted to the Embassy at London a telegram<anchor
                        n="60" xml:id="d357-f1"/> setting forth background information concerning
                    steps taken by the American Presbyterian Mission to resume its educational work
                    in Iran and concerning the invitation extended by the Iranian Government to Dr.
                    Monroe to conduct an educational survey. This telegram contained the following
                    paragraph: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Please seek an early opportunity to express to the Foreign Office the
                            sympathetic interest of this Government in the two proposed educational
                            undertakings in Iran and state that it would be greatly appreciated if
                            appropriate British officials in Iran might be specifically instructed
                            to lend their support thereto.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <pb facs="0391" n="383" xml:id="pg383"/>
                <p>You should inform your British colleague of the nature of the request being made
                    to the British Government and discuss with him preliminary steps which might be
                    taken in regard to the matter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[The British Minister in Iran was instructed on January 9 by the British
                        Foreign Office to support the United States position in Iran with respect to
                        both of these projects. Although the Iranian Cabinet on January 10 “approved
                        in principle” the return of the mission properties, the Mission Board at
                        Tehran, after one formal approach to the Iranian Government, decided not to
                        proceed further with the matter. The Monroe mission failed to get to Iran
                        because of the problem of wartime air transport priorities. (391.1163/126;
                        891.42/99, 105, 111)]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
